1
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:43,032
好的，太好了。嗨，我叫理查德·泰勒。今天由我代课，因为迪克和彼得都出城了。我的嗓子有点哑，所以你们能听清这堂课就算很走运了，但我会尽力而为。他们让我来讲对称群，特别是对称群中的共轭类。
Okay, great. Hi, my name's Richard Taylor. I'm standing in today because both Dick and Peter are out of town, and I'm losing my voice, so you're going to be lucky to finally hear this lecture, but we'll see what I can do. So they asked me to talk about the symmetric group, and in particular, conjugacy classes in the symmetric group.

2
00:00:43,032 --> 00:00:46,590
我想你们已经——让我先带大家回顾一下对称群。
And so I think you've already—let me start by reminding you about the symmetric group.

3
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:58,034
我想这些你们大多已经知道了，所以如果我讲到你们不熟悉的内容，请随时告诉我。
I think you know most of this, so tell me if I'm saying things that you are not familiar with.

4
00:00:58,034 --> 00:01:27,818
按惯例，我们用 S_n 表示 n 个文字上的对称群，它就是从 n 元集合到自身的双射集合。传统上把这些元素标号为 1 到 n，即置换或双射。在我看来，
So it's traditional to write S_n for the symmetric group on n letters, which is the set of bijections from the set of n elements to itself, and traditionally you label those elements 1 to n, so the permutations or bijections.

5
00:01:27,818 --> 00:01:45,195
你们用的教材在这点上做得不太好：书中大部分地方都把映射、函数写成作用在左边，而为了迎合某些惯例，却在对称群这一节突然改变了做法。
It seems to me the book you're using doesn't make a very good job of this: most of the book writes elements, functions acting on the left, and to meet other conventions it suddenly changes that in this section on the symmetric group.

6
00:01:45,195 --> 00:02:02,900
不管怎样，在我看来在书的中间部分改变记号是很愚蠢的，因为这只会把人搞糊涂。但不管怎样，我就按书上的来吧。这些置换将作用在右边，这意味着只要我记得，
Anyway, it seems to me silly to change in the middle of the book, because it's just going to confuse people, but anyway, I'll do what the book does. So these permutations are going to act on the right,

7
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:30,358
我就会把作用写成 i P 而不是 P(i)。这样做的效果是，如果先用 P 作用于 i，再用 Q 作用，就等于用乘积 PQ 作用于 i。关于对称群，我还应该提醒大家哪些事情呢？
which means I'm going to write i P as long as I remember to do this, rather than P(i), and this has the effect that if you first act on i by P and then on Q, it's the same as acting on i by the product PQ. What else should I remind you about?

8
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:47,959
对于置换或对称群中的元素，有两种记法：第一种就是简单地列出每个元素映到哪里。
So then there are two notations for permutations or elements of the symmetric group: the first is simply to give a list of where all the elements go.

9
00:02:47,959 --> 00:03:08,608
比如对于 6 个文字上的对称群的一个元素，如果把 1 映到 3，我就在 1 下面写 3，来表示 1 映到 3；然后可能有 2 映到 6，3 映到 5，4 映到 4，5映到 1，6 映到 2。
So if I had an element of the symmetric group on six letters which sent 1 to 3, I would write 3 underneath the 1 to show that 1 goes to 3; and then we might have 2 to 6, 3 to 5, 4 to 4, 5 to 1, and 6 to 2.

10
00:03:08,608 --> 00:03:17,775
好的，这个置换把这一行的元素映到那一行的对应元素，我会经常使用这种记法。让我把这个置换称为 P。
Okay, so this is the permutation that sends each element of this row to the element of that row, and I'm going to be using that or not.

11
00:03:17,775 --> 00:03:39,989
为了复习一下它的运算，再取第二个置换 Q：第一行是 1 2 3 4 5 6，第二行是 2 1 4 5 6 3。
So let me call that particular permutation P. And just to review how this works, let me have a second permutation Q, which will be 1 2 3 4 5 6 2 1 4 5 6 3.

12
00:03:39,989 --> 00:04:27,530
如果我想求乘积 PQ，你们熟悉怎么计算这样的乘积吗？有人在摇头？抱歉，好的。
And so if I'm interested in the product PQ, you're familiar with how you would calculate a product like that? Somebody shake their head? Sorry, right.

13
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:34,650
那么在右作用下，1 会变成什么？
So what would happen to 1 under—because we're writing the action on the right?

14
00:04:34,650 --> 00:05:01,205
如果看元素 1——好的，你们以前熟悉这种两行形式写置换的记法吗？我明白了，好的。此前别人告诉我你们对这个很熟悉，抱歉。
So if I look at 1—okay, were you familiar with this notation for writing permutations, these two rows in this way? I see, yeah. Okay, so I had understood from what I had been told that you were familiar with this, I'm sorry.

15
00:05:01,205 --> 00:05:08,499
没关系，这只是一种记录置换作用的方式：追踪每个元素映到哪里。
Right, so it's just a way of writing what the permutation does: you just want to keep track of where every element goes.

16
00:05:08,499 --> 00:05:24,087
第一行写要置换的元素——这是 6 个文字上的对称群的一个元素——而在第二行写它们分别映到哪里：1 映到 3，2 映到 6，3 映到 5，4 映到 4，5 映到 1，6 映到2。
So in the first row you write the elements that you're going to permute—this will be an element of the symmetric group on six letters—and on the second row you write where they're going to go: so 1 goes to 3, 2 goes to 6, 3 goes to 5, 4 goes to 4, 5 to 1, 6 goes to 2.

17
00:05:24,087 --> 00:05:31,994
如果我想计算两个这种置换的乘积，该怎么做？
So if I want to figure out a product of two such things, what do I have to do?

18
00:05:31,994 --> 00:05:48,470
我必须算出1 映到哪里：算出 1 在乘积 PQ 下的像，这等价于 1 先被 P 作用，再被 Q 作用。
I have to figure out where 1 goes: I have to figure out what's the image of 1 under the product PQ, which is the same as 1 acted on by P and then acted on by Q.

19
00:05:48,470 --> 00:05:59,389
1 在 P 作用下映到 3，接着在 Q 作用下 3 映到 4，所以是 4。
So 1 under P goes to 3, and then under Q, 3 goes on to 4, so it's 4.

20
00:05:59,389 --> 00:06:17,556
类似地，2 在 P 作用下映到 6，在 Q 作用下 6映到 3，所以我在 2 下面写 3。有人能告诉我 3 下面写什么吗？
Similarly, 2 under P goes to 6, and then under Q, 6 goes on to 3, so I would write a 3 here. So does somebody want to tell me what I write underneath 3?

21
00:06:17,556 --> 00:06:42,820
6，谢谢，是 6；4 先映到 4 再映到 5；5 先映到 1 再映到 2；6 先映到 2 再映到 1，如果我没算错的话。好的，这就是置换的一种记法，非常直接。
6, thank you, 6; and 4 goes to 4, goes to 5; 5 goes to 1, goes to 2; 6 goes to 2, goes to 1, if I haven't made a mistake. Okay, so this is one notation for permutations, very straightforward.

22
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:52,750
还有第二种重要的记法，就是轮换记法。大家学过轮换记法吗？有人点头了。
There's a second important notation, which is the cycle notation. So have you met the cycle notation? Someone said yes.

23
00:06:52,750 --> 00:07:11,825
看来出于某种原因，他们先讲了轮换记法，而没讲这种更容易的记法。在轮换记法中，你能更直观地看清实际发生了什么。
So for some reason they've talked about the cycle notation and not the easier one. Okay, so in the cycle notation, you somehow think more about what's actually happening.

24
00:07:11,825 --> 00:07:17,858
比如看元素 1，考察置换 P：P 把 1 怎么变？
So you have the point 1, and let's look at that permutation P: what does P do to 1?

25
00:07:17,858 --> 00:07:39,135
1 映到 3；接着看 3，3 映到5——抱歉，在 P 下 3 映到 5，而 5 又映回 1。
1 goes to 3, and then if you look at 3, 3 goes to 5—oh sorry, 3 goes to 5 under P, and 5 goes back to 1.

26
00:07:39,135 --> 00:07:54,397
所以如果你反复施加 P，1 映到 3，映到 5，映回 1，就会在这三个点之间循环轮换。再看——我们还漏掉了什么？
So if you keep applying P, you just go, and 1 goes to 3, goes to 5, goes to 1, it's just going to cycle around these three points. And if you look at—so what are we missing?

27
00:07:54,397 --> 00:08:08,480
还没看 2：2 会发生什么？2 映到 6，然后 6 映回 2。
We haven't got to 2 yet: so what will happen to 2? 2 will go to 6, and then 6 will go back to 2.

28
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:16,059
所以2 映到 6，再映回 2；如果反复施加 P，就会在这两个点之间循环轮换。
So we have 2 going to 6, and then that will go back to 2, so if you keep applying P, you're just going to keep cycling around these two points.

29
00:08:16,059 --> 00:08:21,975
最后还有点 4，它保持不动，在 P 下映到自身。
And then finally there's the point 4, which is just left fixed, it goes to itself when you apply P.

30
00:08:21,975 --> 00:08:56,429
我们用所谓的轮换记法来记录它：用括号中的序列表示 P 的这些轮换或轨道：1 映到 3 映到 5 映回 1；2映到 6 映回 2；4 保持不动：(1 3 5)(2 6)(4)。好的，这就是 P 的另一种记法，所谓的轮换记法。
And you record this in the so-called cycle notation: you just write strings in parentheses for these cycles or the orbits that you get of P: 1 goes to 3 goes to 5 goes back to 1; 2 goes to 6 goes back to 2; 4 stays where it is: (1 3 5)(2 6)(4). Okay, so this is another, the so-called cycle notation for P.

31
00:08:56,429 --> 00:09:00,942
这样写存在一定的不唯一性。为什么？
And there's a certain amount of ambiguity when you write this. Why?

32
00:09:00,942 --> 00:09:19,870
我的意思是，用轮换记法写 P 并不唯一：我可以把各个轮换按不同的顺序排列；在每个轮换内部，我也可以重排文字的顺序：比如也可以写成 (5 1 3)，
I mean, there's not a unique way of writing P in cycle notation: I can put the cycles in different orders, and within each cycle I can rearrange the order of the letters: I could also write this as (5 1 3),

33
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:38,287
可以循环轮换它们，因为 5映到 1 映到 3，这取决于从这个三角形的哪个点起步。如果有一个 1-轮换，可以直接省略它，这并不会有任何影响。
I can cyclically permute these because 5 goes to 1 goes to 3, it depends where in this triangle I start. If I have a 1-cycle, I can just drop it, it doesn't really make any difference.

34
00:09:38,287 --> 00:09:53,303
而且各个轮换按什么顺序写也无关紧要，因为它们不包含公共数字：这个只移动 5、1 和 3，而那个只移动 2 和 6。
And it doesn't matter what order I write the cycles in, they don't involve any common numbers: this only moves 5, 1, and 3, and this only moves 2 and 6.

35
00:09:53,303 --> 00:10:02,670
所以存在一定的不唯一性，但也仅此而已。
So there's a certain amount of ambiguity, but that's the limit of the ambiguity.

36
00:10:12,879 --> 00:10:48,857
基本事实是：任何置换都可以唯一地写成不相交轮换的乘积——“不相交”意味着它们没有公共数字，任何数字都不会同时出现在两个轮换中—
So the basic fact is that any permutation can be written uniquely as a product of disjoint cycles—disjoint meaning they have no numbers in common, no number occurs in both cycles—

37
00:10:48,857 --> 00:11:36,501
—在允许我刚才解释的几种调整的前提下是唯一的：可以重排各个轮换，循环轮换单个轮换内部的元素，也可以省略 1-轮换。
disjoint cycles, up to the various switches I explained you could make: you can reorder the cycles, cyclically permute the elements in a cycle, and you can drop 1-cycles.

38
00:11:36,501 --> 00:11:58,725
有时人们会约定必须把 1-轮换全部写出来，但那样做很费时间。好的，大家对这个熟悉吗？熟悉。并且你们可以用这种方式计算乘积。
Sometimes people make the convention that you always have to put them in, but it's just time consuming to do that. Okay, so is this familiar to you? Yes. And you can calculate products in this way.

39
00:11:58,725 --> 00:12:16,806
于是在这种记法下，置换 Q 就是：它把 1 映到 2 又映回 1；把 3 映到 4，4 映到 5，5 映到 6，再映回 3。
So in this notation, then Q would be: it sends 1 to 2 which goes back to 1; 3 to 4, 4 to 5, 5 to 6, back to 3.

40
00:12:16,806 --> 00:12:36,616
所以这就是Q 的不相交轮换分解：(1 2)(3 4 5 6)。你可以重新计算乘积 PQ，即 (1 3 5)(2 6) 乘以 (1 2)(3 4 5 6)。
So this is the cycle decomposition of Q: (1 2)(3 4 5 6). And you can calculate again the product PQ as (1 3 5)(2 6) times (1 2)(3 4 5 6).

41
00:12:37,770 --> 00:13:06,030
那么用轮换表示时该怎么计算乘积呢？这是大家练习过的吗？没有？好的。出于某种原因，让我修正一下，就用我原本写的形式：(1 3 5)，写什么顺序无所谓，接着是 (2 6)。
So how do you work out the product when you work in cycles? Is this something you've practiced doing? No? Okay. So for some reason, let me correct this, let me just use the original form I had for this thing: (1 3 5), it doesn't matter, (2 6).

42
00:13:06,030 --> 00:13:15,604
我想把它写成不相交轮换的乘积：必须选一个起点，选哪都行，让我选择从 1 开始。
Okay, so I want to write it as a product of cycles: I have to choose to start somewhere, it doesn't matter, let me choose to start with 1.

43
00:13:15,604 --> 00:13:20,705
我想找到包含 1 的轮换：如果施加乘积 PQ，1 映到哪里？
I want to find the cycle involving 1: so where does 1 go if I apply the product PQ?

44
00:13:20,705 --> 00:13:26,230
因为我们是从右边作用：所以 1 首先映到 3。
Well, we're acting from the right: so 1 first of all goes to 3.

45
00:13:26,230 --> 00:13:34,100
我顺着找 1，在这里找到了它，它移到了 3；现在得到了 3，我继续往后找看还有没有 3，看它又移到哪里。
I look along for a 1, I find it here, it moves to 3; I've now got a 3, and I look along to find anywhere else it might be, and see where that moves.

46
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:43,788
下一次找到 3 是在这里，它移到了 4。接着往后看没有 4 了，所以最终落在4。
The next time I find a 3 is here, it moves to a 4. Then I look along and there are no more 4s, so it ends up at 4.

47
00:13:43,788 --> 00:13:52,703
然后我从 4 开始，看它移到哪里：对于 4，我往后看直到找到 4。
Then I'm going to start with 4 and see where this moves to: so for 4, I look along until I find a 4.

48
00:13:52,703 --> 00:14:02,810
第一个出现 4 的地方是在这里：4 移到了 5，后面没有 5 了，所以最终落在 5。
The first place I find it is here: that 4 moves to a 5, and I don't see any more 5s, so that will end up at 5.

49
00:14:02,810 --> 00:14:13,600
接下来我想找出 5 映到哪里：我顺着看，第一个出现 5 的地方在这里。5 映到哪里？它循环回到了 1。
I then want to find out where 5 goes to: so I look along here, the first place I find a 5 is here. Where does the 5 go? It's cycled back to 1.

50
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:28,339
好的，现在得到了 1，我继续往后找 1：下一个 1 在这里，它映到 2，后面没有 2 了，所以最终落在 2。现在我想问 2 映到哪里。
Okay, so now I've got a 1, I move along again to look for another 1: the next 1 is here, that goes to a 2, and there are no more 2s, so it ends up at 2. Now I want to ask where 2 goes to.

51
00:14:28,339 --> 00:14:40,380
好的，从 2 开始：第一个移动 2 的是什么？是这个 2-轮换：它把 2 移到 6。现在得到了 6；还有别的移动 6 吗？
Okay, so I start with 2: what's the first thing that tells me to move a 2? It's this 2-cycle: it's going to move the 2 to the 6. I've now got a 6; is anything else going to move a 6?

52
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:45,641
这里有个 6，它被移回 3。后面没有移动 3 的了，所以我得到 3。
Here's a 6, it's going to be moved back to a 3. Nothing else will move a 3, so I get 3.

53
00:14:45,641 --> 00:14:53,247
所以我总是向右移动，每当该数字出现时就转换它。现在到了哪里？
So I'm always moving to the right and switching something every time that number occurs. So where have I got to?

54
00:14:53,247 --> 00:15:07,664
3：我往后看，第一个3 在这里，这个轮换把它移到 5。现在得到了 5；继续往后，下一个看到 5 的地方在这里，它被移到 6。
3: I look along, the first 3 is here, this cycle will move it to a 5. I've now got a 5; move along, the next place I see a 5 is here, which is moved to a 6.

55
00:15:07,664 --> 00:15:24,020
有了 6；往后看，第一个 6 在这里，它被移到 2；再顺着找 2，这里有个 2，它被移到 1；往后看没有 1 了，所以最终是 1。而我们一开始就是 1，所以它现在循环闭合了。
There's 6; look along, the first 6 I see is here, it's moved to a 2; look along for a 2, there's a 2 here, it's moved to a 1; look along, there are no more 1s, so that's a 1, and we already had a 1, so it's now going to cycle back on itself.

56
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:49,631
因此乘积 PQ 就是一个 6-轮换，如果运气好的话，这正好符合我们之前两行记法算出的结果：1 到 4，4 到 5，5 到 2，2 到 3，3 到 6，6 到 1。所以它完全吻合我们之前做的计算。
So the product PQ is just one 6-cycle, and with a bit of luck this agrees with what we had here: 1 to 4, 4 to 5, 5 to 2, 2 to 3, 3 to 6, 6 to 1. So it does agree with what we did before.

57
00:15:49,631 --> 00:16:28,755
好的，大家都明白了吗？还是需要我再做一个例子？有人不想让我再讲一个，有人不吭声。都清楚了吗？好的，太棒了。顺便问一下，P^6 是什么？是恒等置换，对吧。你们是怎么看出来的？
Okay, is that clear to everybody, or do you want me to do another one? Some people don't want me to do another one, some people aren't saying anything. Is that clear? Yeah, great. What's P to the sixth by the way? It's the identity, right. How did you see that?

58
00:16:28,755 --> 00:16:42,158
是的，没错：这个元素是不相交轮换的乘积，它们彼此对易，因为不相交轮换没有公共元素，它们是对易的。
Yeah, that's right: this element is a product of things that commute with each other, because disjoint cycles, cycles with no common element, commute.

59
00:16:42,158 --> 00:16:51,553
正如我刚才解释的，我可以重排它们的顺序：先写 (2 6) 还是先写 (1 3 5) 都无所谓，它们对易是因为它们没有公共元素。
As I explained here, I can reorder them: it doesn't matter whether I do the (2 6) first or the (1 3 5) first, these things commute because they've got no common element.

60
00:16:51,553 --> 00:17:03,281
因此如果把它升到 6 次方，就等于分别把它们升到 6 次方：这是一个 3-轮换，施加三次就得到恒等置换；这是一个 2-轮换，施加两次就得到恒等置换。
And so if I raise it to the sixth power, it's like raising this to the sixth power and this to the sixth power: this is a 3-cycle, so when I do it three times I get the identity; this is a 2-cycle, so when I do it twice I get the identity.

61
00:17:03,281 --> 00:17:08,116
所以当施加六次时，这个是恒等置换，那个也是恒等置换，而 1-轮换本来就是恒等置换。
So when I do it six times, this is the identity, this is the identity, and this 1-cycle always was the identity.

62
00:17:08,116 --> 00:17:20,410
或者你也可以从图象上理解：施加 P 时，元素在这个三角形中轮换；如果施加 3 的任意倍数次，三角形中的每个点都会固定不动；如果施加2 的任意倍数次，这里的两个点也都会固定不动。
Or you can think sort of pictorially: as I do P, I move around this triangle; if I do it any multiple of three times, everything in this triangle will be fixed; if I do any multiple of two times, everything here will be fixed.

63
00:17:20,410 --> 00:17:42,616
这在某种程度上展现了轮换记法的美妙之处：你能非常迅速地看出这种性质，而如果我只是写出——刚才我擦掉了——写出 Q 的两行记法并问大家 Q^4 是多少，仅从那个表格来看是完全看不出来的，你只能老老实实硬算。
And this somehow illustrates the beauty of the cycle notation: you can very quickly see things like this, whereas if I just wrote down—well I've erased it—when I wrote down Q equals this, and asked you what Q to the fourth was, from that table it would be completely hopeless, I mean you'd just have to do the calculation.

64
00:17:42,616 --> 00:17:54,830
但一旦把它写成这种轮换形式，你就能立刻看出 Q^4 是恒等置换，因为它是相互对易的一个 2-轮换与一个 4-轮换的乘积。
